(7453194, 1179583, 136989, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>What a beautiful location indeed!  I am always a sucker for tree-lined roads or trails, so it is rather fitting that your image wind up with me (and for my first critique too!).  <br/>The road and lines of trees definitely draw the eye to the sun and illustrate that you did meet the challenge criteria for contre-jour.  The backlight from the sun lends a warm glow to the vibrant autumn colors and the blue sky helps balance out what might have been a whole lot of orange.  Im not a huge fan of the sun-spot-circle, as its size and opacity are a bit distracting from the overall scene.  Yet, there is something appealing about that full circle  maybe its a portal to another dimension?  <br/> <br/>In terms of the faux autumn processing  overall it seems to work well.  I am wondering if the processing might have compromised some of the details though.  Some of the grass and leaves on the left look a little chunky to me but that could also be an effect of the bright light from the sun.  Just an observation as this does not detract much from the shot at all. Nicely done!  If you need me, Ill be following the road off into the sunset.<br/> <br/>~Cia<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! What a beautiful location indeed!  I am always a sucker for tree-lined roads or trails, so it is rather fitting that your image wind up with me (and for my first critique too!).  The road and lines of trees definitely draw the eye to the sun and illustrate that you did meet the challenge criteria for contre-jour.  The backlight from the sun lends a warm glow to the vibrant autumn colors and the blue sky helps balance out what might have been a whole lot of orange.  Im not a huge fan of the sun-spot-circle, as its size and opacity are a bit distracting from the overall scene.  Yet, there is something appealing about that full circle  maybe its a portal to another dimension?   In terms of the faux autumn processing  overall it seems to work well.  I am wondering if the processing might have compromised some of the details though.  Some of the grass and leaves on the left look a little chunky to me but that could also be an effect of the bright light from the sun.  Just an observation as this does not detract much from the shot at all. Nicely done!  If you need me, Ill be following the road off into the sunset. ~Cia', '2016-05-03 01:06:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7454923, 1179593, 113591, '<td valign="top">I''ve tried these shots, they do not come out like this. Explain yourself. Hehe.</td>', 'I''ve tried these shots, they do not come out like this. Explain yourself. Hehe.', '2016-05-16 02:53:44.000000', NULL, 0),
